# Accessibility and motion

## Baseline a11y

- Target **WCAG AA** contrast on text and interactive controls.
- Global `:focus-visible` outline; remove default `:focus` ring only when `:focus-visible` replaces it.
- **Skip to main content**: `<button type="button">` (not `<a>`) so Space and Enter both work; hidden off-screen until `:focus-visible`; target `<main id="..." tabIndex={-1}>`.
- Section-specific skip links when nav chrome differs (e.g. sidebar vs top navbar).
- Set `scroll-margin-top` on skip targets under fixed headers.
- Correct `cursor` on interactive vs text inputs (pointer vs text).

## Interactive parity

- **Hover and `:focus-visible` must match** for buttons and controls — keyboard users get the same affordance as mouse users.
- Use `:is(:hover, :focus-visible)` in CSS for shared treatment.
- Disabled controls: no transform/glow; `cursor: not-allowed`; clear `opacity`.

## Motion (UX Engineer bar)

- Motion must **communicate state** (feedback, hierarchy, continuity) — not decorate.
- Animate **`transform` and `opacity`** first; avoid layout-thrashing properties when possible.
- Timing: ~100–200ms small UI, ~220–350ms panels, longer only for deliberate “moments”.
- Include **`:active` press** feedback (brief scale/shadow compress).
- Always provide `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` fallbacks — color/border only, no transform/shimmer.
- Prefer **CSS-first** animations; add JS libraries only when orchestration truly requires it.

## Shared button motion pattern

- Base class + variant modifiers (`hero-action-btn`, `--primary`, `--secondary`, `--ghost`).
- Primary: lift + glow + optional shimmer via `::before`.
- Secondary: softer lift + border bloom.
- Themed contexts: separate variant (e.g. `--primary-themed`) when hover colors must respect CSS variables.
